usage: rogue_one_runner.py [-h] [--sample_folder SAMPLE_FOLDER] [--timeouts]
                           [--no_redo] [--single SINGLE] [--fast]
                           [--log_level LOG_LEVEL] [--raise_all] [--save_odrg]

Runner for mass parallel analysis.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --sample_folder SAMPLE_FOLDER
                        A folder containing folders of datasets, each of which
                        has folders of before/after update pairs. e.g. given S
                        amples/30_backstabber_samples/pack_0.1--
                        >pack_0.2/pack_0.1/ as a sample, the argument should
                        be just Samples, so that the samples are captured by
                        **/*-->**/
  --timeouts
  --no_redo
  --single SINGLE       A folder containing a single package pair to be
                        analyzed.
  --fast                Coarser analysis for post-timeout reanalysis attempt.
  --log_level LOG_LEVEL
                        More or less verbose logs: DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR,
                        FATAL
  --raise_all
  --save_odrg           Save the ODRGs built for the before and after versions
                        of the program. Saves as GraphML in files
                        <pair_dir>/before.graphml and after.graphml.
